; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR MOONBASE  -  a text adventure   (VM1 @ $4000, SETSIZE 3)
; ==========================================================================
; A moonquake has wrecked Moonbase Tycho. The crew got away without you, the
; air is running out, and the last lander is out on the crater floor. Get to
; it and get it off the ground.
;
; Type commands of one or two words: N, S, E, W, UP, DOWN, IN, OUT, LOOK,
; INVENTORY (I), TAKE WRENCH, DROP, EXAMINE LOCKER, OPEN, READ, WEAR, USE,
; TURN ON FLASHLIGHT, PUSH, TYPE, HELP, QUIT. Any case. Only the first four
; letters of a word count. Every move uses air.
;
; EVERY GAME IS DIFFERENT. Press a key at the title and the moment you press it
; seeds the shuffle: the flashlight, wrench, spacesuit and log start in random
; places (the locker is one of them - it may hold several things, or nothing),
; the airlock code is a new 4-digit number (the commander's log has it), the air
; and the suit's tank vary, the opening varies, and every room has one of two
; descriptions. PLAY AGAIN shuffles again. Every layout can be won: nothing you
; need to cross the dark tunnel starts beyond it.
;
; 10 rooms, 16 objects (5 to carry), 133 words. The parser is native 1802 at
; $4C00 (Firmware-Math/adventure_native.asm, 382 bytes, run with RUNMC after
; each line); the game is the STELLAR program below. Edit the world - rooms,
; exits, objects, words, messages - in Firmware-Math/build_adventure.py.
;
; MEMORY. SETSIZE 3 takes $4000-$6FFF: program, parser, the world and the
; messages ($5280-$6FFF). The variables, the shuffled state and the typed line are
; at $7100-$71FF in VM4's block (SETSIZE cannot take a fourth); $7000, VM4's
; START byte, is kept $00 so no program can start there.
; Everything the game changes is reset at the start of each game, so it can be
; played again without reloading.
; Needs SETSIZE ($F2), RUNMC ($F1), PRINTSTR ($C1), GETSTR ($C2): V0061.28 on.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/adventure_verify.py, V0061.34 image): PASS, 63 checks - 12 shuffled games each won (12 layouts, 12 codes, both openings, both descriptions of every room), PLAY AGAIN reshuffles, parser + rules on a pinned layout, both deaths
;
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-09-26 - Craig: "It works!" - v1, and
; then this shuffled v2, the same day.
;
; 730 STELLAR commands, $4000-$4928 (2345 bytes).
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START                              Start of program, and run the label pre-pass
; D 4001 F2 03          SETSIZE 3                          Take $4000-$6FFF: VM1 plus the two blocks above it
; D 4003 11 0B 00 00    LOADXI R11 0000                    RB = 0: the index for flags
; D 4007 11 0E 31 80    LOADXI R14 3180
; D 400B 10 00 00       LOADAI 0000
